1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,520
Calf pain that starts with walking

2
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:02,500
and eases with rest

3
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,300
is a pattern doctors don't ignore.

4
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,940
Let's see what Dr. Rahim says.

5
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,500
Calf pain or cramping while walking,

6
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:08,480
this is called claudication

7
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:09,740
or intermittent claudication.

8
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:11,260
It happens when narrowing arteries

9
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:12,800
reduce blood flow to the leg muscles

10
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,680
during activity.

11
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,720
The muscles essentially run low on oxygen.

12
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,160
The pain usually eases with rest

13
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:19,040
and then returns with walking again.

14
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,160
This pattern is a known early signal

15
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,940
of peripheral arterial disease,

16
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,600
which is directly connected
to the cardiovascular risk.

17
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,600
The signal doctors watch the most

18
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,620
is claudication,

19
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:29,700
that is, calf pain

20
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,680
that appears during activity or walking

21
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:32,960
and disappears with rest.

22
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,280
It is considered one of the most

23
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,960
clinically significant early signals.

24
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:37,300
But if this intermittent claudication

25
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,980
converts into continuous pain,
even at rest,

26
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:41,500
this occurs in patients who have got

27
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,600
critical [limb] ischemia,

28
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,340
which is a serious state of affairs

29
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:45,940
for peripheral vascular disease.

30
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:47,900
It suggests that arterial blood flow

31
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,400
is already reduced enough

32
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:50,640
to affect muscle function,

33
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,360
and research consistently shows

34
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,720
that people with claudication

35
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,340
have elevated cardiovascular risk.

36
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,760
That is why doctors

37
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,880
don't dismiss leg pain during walking.

38
00:00:58,880 --> 00:00:59,700
They always,

39
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,580
always investigate.
